s_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.014201140108140484,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5828779938902677,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":2.9,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.24354608195878014,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.05410505092453263,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":15.3,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0935325335397642,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":2.6,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.011678086000717958,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":19.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.011450670974360921,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":30.7,"_gate_margins":0.02199520422271281,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":72.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04623747332284039,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":62.5,"_gate_share_shrink":0.1572074741714331,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.022712777485371063,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":62.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.00983,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Rayonier Inc. is a land resources real estate investment trust (REIT) with a portfolio comprising over four million acres in the U.S. South and U.S. Northwest. The company is focused on managing its timberlands on a sustainable basis while optimizing its overall portfolio value by delivering land to its highest and best use. Rayonier also operates six sawmills, an industrial-grade plywood mill, residential and commercial real estate developments, and a rural land sales program. Rayonier is committed to corporate responsibility, third-party forest certification, and supporting climate change mitigation through its land-based solutions business. Rayonier Inc. was established in 1926 and was incorporated in North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark D. McHugh J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 285 people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue falling 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $39K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Rayonier Inc. REIT is a mid-cap real estate business with a $6.4B market cap on $484M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -19% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +6.4% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To Rayonier (RYN) Bigger Buyback Plan","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-ryn/rayonier/news/how-investors-are-reacting-to-rayonier-ryn-bigger-buyback-pl","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794472035.105,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (RYN) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/Understanding_the_Setup:_RYN_and_Scalable_Risk_110926115801_1794243481.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794243481.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Rayonier (RYN) 